QuestGuidance.Register("en",346,{
[11041]="70053FFE\n1\tTalk to Dwalin to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the Introduction and be transported to Thorin's Gate, speak with Dwalin.\n",
[11042]="70054FD3\n1\tSpeak with Núluzagar to bypass the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience, speak with Núluzagar again.\n",
[11043]="7006685B\n1\tTalk to your friend Valaric Túcca to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Mossward following the defeat of Madthrug, speak to your friend Valaric Túcca in Lyndelby.\n",
[11044]="70066D5C\n1\tTalk to Bevan at the gate of Mossward to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Mossward following the defeat of Madthrug, speak to Bevan at the gate of Mossward.\n",
[11045]="700196CD\n1\tTalk to Glóin to skip the Tutorial\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the tutorial experience and be transported to Thorin's Gate at the outset of the game's story, speak with Glóin again.\n",
[11046]="700196CE\n1\tTalk to Talagan Silvertongue to skip the Tutorial\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the tutorial experience and be transported to Edhelion following the rise of the Dourhands, speak with Talagan Silvertongue again.\n",
[11047]="700196CF\n1\tTalk to Postman Took to skip the Tutorial\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the tutorial experience and be transported to Archet at the outset of the Blackwold incursion, speak with Postman Took again.\n",
[11048]="7001CD79\n1\tTalk to the shade\tA shade has appeared within the Barrow-downs. Speak with him to discover why he is here.\n2\tSurvive for as long as possible\tThe Barrow-downs have unleashed their fury. Hold your position for as long as you can possibly stand.\n",
[11049]="70052505\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tComplete Skirmish Assaults across Middle-earth (total: 10)\tHarbingers of the Dead have appeared in Skirmishes throughout Middle-earth. You should seek out and defeat Harbingers of the Dead. NOTE: This quest can be advanced by completing 'Skirmish Assault: Strongholds of the Free Peoples', 'Skirmish Assault: Treacherous Wilds', 'Skirmish Assault: Beneath the World', or 'Skirmish Assault: Shadows of Dol Guldur'.\n3\tTalk to Nedda Pinleaf in Bree, Ost Galadh, or the Twenty-first Hall\tNedda Pinleaf can be found the Skirmish Camps of Bree, Ost Galadh, and the Twenty-first Hall. You should return to Nedda Pinleaf.\n",
[11050]="7001B807\n1\tSpeak to Fantus\tSpeak to Fantus to get your skirmish marks.\n",
[11051]="7005237D\n1\tComplete 'Ill Omens: Battle of the Twenty-first Hall'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Battle of the Deep-way'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Battle of the Way of Smiths'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Rescue in Nûrz Ghâshu'\tNedda Pinleaf has asked you to seek out Harbingers of the Dead in the depths of Middle-earth. NOTE: Harbingers of the Dead can be found in the following skirmishes: Battle of the Twenty-first Hall, Battle of the Deep-way, Battle of the Way of Smiths, and Rescue in Nûrz Ghâshu. You only need to complete three of the four listed quests today to advance this quest.\n2\tTalk to Nedda Pinleaf\tNedda Pinleaf can be found at the skirmish camps of Bree, Ost Galadh, and the Twenty-first Hall. You should talk to Nedda Pinleaf.\n",
[11052]="7005237E\n1\tComplete 'Ill Omens: Breaching the Necromancer's Gate'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Assault on the Ringwraiths' Lair'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: The Battle in the Tower'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Strike Against Dannenglor'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Protectors of Thangúlhad'\tNedda Pinleaf has asked you to seek out Harbingers of the Dead among the more treacherous wilds of Middle-earth. NOTE: Harbingers of the Dead can be found in the following skirmishes: Breaching the Necromancer's Gate, Assault on the Ringwraiths' Lair, The Battle in the Tower, Strike Against Dannenglor, and Protectors of Thangúlhad. You only need to complete four of the five listed quests today to advance this quest.\n2\tTalk to Nedda Pinleaf\tNedda Pinleaf can be found at the skirmish camps of Bree, Ost Galadh, and the Twenty-first Hall. You should talk to Nedda Pinleaf.\n",
[11053]="70052312\n1\tComplete 'Ill Omens: Defence of The Prancing Pony'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Thievery and Mischief'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Trouble in Tuckborough'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Siege of Gondamon'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Stand at Amon Sûl'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Doom of Caras Gelebren'\tNedda Pinleaf has asked you to seek out Harbingers of the Dead near the Strongholds of the Free Peoples. NOTE: Harbingers of the Dead can be found in the following skirmishes: Defence of The Prancing Pony, Thievery and Mischief, Trouble in Tuckborough, Siege of Gondamon, Stand at Amon Sûl, and Doom of Caras Gelebren. You only need to complete four of the six listed quests today to advance this quest.\n2\tTalk to Nedda Pinleaf\tNedda Pinleaf can be found at the skirmish camps of Bree, Ost Galadh, and the Twenty-first Hall. You should talk to Nedda Pinleaf.\n",
[11054]="7005237F\n1\tComplete 'Ill Omens: Storm on Methedras'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Ford of Bruinen'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: The Icy Crevasse'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Attack At Dawn'\030Complete 'Ill Omens: Barrow-downs'\tNedda Pinleaf has asked you to seek out Harbingers of the Dead among the more treacherous wilds of Middle-earth. NOTE: Harbingers of the Dead can be found in the following Skirmishes: Storm on Methedras, Ford of Bruinen, The Icy Crevasse, Attack At Dawn, and Survival: Barrow-downs. You only need to complete four of the five listed quests today to advance this quest.\n2\tTalk to Nedda Pinleaf\tNedda Pinleaf can be found at the skirmish camps of Bree, Ost Galadh, and the Twenty-first Hall. You should talk to Nedda Pinleaf.\n",
[11055]="7001B574\n1\tTalk to Trennor\tSpeak with Trennor to learn the skirmish traits and skills.\n",
[11056]="700242AD\n1\tTalk to Brogur in the Deep-way\tBrogur is leading the defence of the Deep-way against the forces of Mazog. You should report to him to receive your assignment.\n2\tPush back the first assault\tThe first assault on the Deep-way has begun. Protect the barricades!\n3\tPush back the second assault\tThe second assault on the Deep-way has begun. Protect the barricades!\n4\tPush back the third assault\tThe third assault on the Deep-way has begun. Defend the barricades!\n5\tPush back the fourth assault\tThe fourth assault on the Deep-way has begun. Defend the barricades!\n6\tPush back the final assault\tThe final assault has begun. The enemy's numbers are waning, but their ferocity increases. Withstand this assault, defeat their leader, and maintain control of the Deep-way.\n",
[11057]="70024A9A\n1\tTalk to Stóthkell in the Way of Smiths\tStóthkell is leading the defence of the Way of Smiths against the forces of Mazog. You should report to him to receive your assignment.\n2\tPush back the first assault\tThe first assault on the Way of Smiths has begun. Protect the forges!\n3\tPush back the second assault\tThe second assault on the Way of Smiths has begun. Protect the forges!\n4\tPush back the final assault\tThe final assault has begun. The enemy's numbers are waning, but their ferocity increases. Withstand this assault, defeat their leader, and maintain control of the Deep-way.\n5\tTalk to Stóthkell atop the Supervisor's Platform\tThere is a pause in the battle. You should talk to Stóthkell on the Supervisor's Platform.\n6\tDefeat Harna and his keepers\tHarna the troll and his keepers are attacking the entrance hall!\n",
[11058]="7001B976\n1\tTalk to Trennor\tSpeak to Trennor to receive your skirmish soldier skill.\n",
[11059]="7001D005\n1\tComplete Thievery and Mischief\tThe Skirmish Captain asked you to aid Second-watcher Heathstraw in reclaiming Bree from bandits and brigands.\n2\tComplete Defence of the Prancing Pony\tThe Skirmish Captain asked you to aid Second-watcher Heathstraw in reclaiming Bree from bandits and brigands.\n3\tTalk to Idhrinnion\tSkirmish camps are at Bree's South Gate, Thorin's Hall, Esteldin, Nimrodel, the Twenty-first Hall, Ost Guruth, Rivendell, Michel Delving, Tinnudir, Suri Kyla, Aughaire, Gwingris and Snowbourn. Bree is safe and secure once more. Report your success back to a Skirmish Captain.\n",
[11060]="7001FEEC\n1\tCollect war-orders ([see journal]/10)\tWar-orders can be found on Orcs, uruks, goblins, trolls, Warg-riders, and more throughout all of Middle-earth. In order to discover where the Enemy plans on striking, the Skirmish Captains need to study some of the war-orders that have been issued to the Enemy's forces. War orders will only drop off of monsters that do not appear grey to your character; they must be around the same level as you\n2\tCollect a Target List\tA Target List can be found on Orcs, uruks, goblins, trolls, Warg-riders, and more throughout all of Middle-earth. In order to discover where the Enemy plans on striking, the Skirmish Captains need to study some of the war-orders that have been issued to the Enemy's forces. War orders will only drop off of monsters that do not appear grey to your character; they must be around the same level as you\n3\tBring the war-orders and target list to a Skirmish Captain at any Skirmish Camp\tReturn the War Orders and Target List to a Skirmish Captain in any of the Skirmish Camps. Skirmish camps are at Bree's South Gate, Thorin's Hall, Esteldin, Nimrodel, the Twenty-first Hall, Ost Guruth, Rivendell, Michel Delving, Tinnudir, Suri Kyla, Aughaire and Gwingris.\n",
[11061]="7001FEEA\n1\tSkirmish camps are at Bree's South-gate, Thorin's Hall, Esteldín, Nimrodel, the Twenty-first Hall, Ost Guruth, Rivendell, Brockenborings, Tinnudír, Sûri Kylä, Aughaire, and Gwingris. You have been instructed to report to the Captain of a Skirmish Camp. Skirmish Camps may be found within every region of Middle-earth.\t\n",
[11062]="7003FFEB\n1\tSearch for the missing hunter near the entrance to Lhingroth\tLhingroth can be found in the hills to the east of Sardol. Amathon has asked you to seek out a missing hunter and investigate the cave of Lhingroth in hopes that the spider threat might be contained.\n2\tExamine the slain hunter outside Lhingroth\tThe slain hunter can be found just outside the rocky entrance of Lhingroth. You have searched the area near Lhingroth and discovered a slain hunter. You should examine his body before pressing on.\n",
[11063]="700306CB\n1\tDefeat stinging black-flies (total: 10)\tStinging black-flies can be found around the Black Heart of Fangorn. You should defeat many stinging black-flies.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have rid the forest of many a harrying, evil insect. This act was a kindness to all inhabitants of Fangorn.\n",
[11064]="70047458\n1\tDefeat Glugor\tThurindol has asked you to investigate Skoironk and find a way to discourage the invaders from remaining there.\n2\tTalk to Thurindol\tYou should return to Thurindol and apprise him of your efforts.\n",
[11065]="70047464\n1\tCollect ore samples\tCollect ore samples within Skoironk.\n2\tCollect ore samples (total: 8)\tCollect ore samples within Skoironk.\n3\tBring the ore samples to Thurindol\tYou should collect ore samples and bring them to Thurindol.\n",
[11066]="70047457\n1\tCollect Rangers' belongings\tCollect Rangers' belongings within Skoironk.\n2\tCollect Rangers' belongings (total: 12)\tCollect Rangers' belongings within Skoironk.\n3\tBring the Ranger belongings to Candúr\tYou should collect Rangers' belongings and bring them to Candúr.\n",
[11067]="7004745C\n1\tDefeat Thrugash\tCandúr has asked you to investigate the Skoironk and find a way to discourage the invaders from remaining there.\n2\tTalk to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.\n",
[11068]="70047462\n1\tDefeat maggots in Skoironk\tDefeat maggots within Skoironk.\n2\tDefeat maggot larvae (total: 12)\tTo weaken the resolve of the invaders within Skoironk, you take it upon yourself to thin their numbers.\n3\tTalk to Thurindol\tYou should return to Thurindol and inform him of your deeds within Skoironk.\n",
[11069]="70047459\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Skoironk\tDefeat Orcs within Skoironk.\n2\tDefeat Orcs (total: 25)\tTo weaken the resolve of the invaders within Skoironk, you take it upon yourself to thin their numbers.\n3\tTalk to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr and inform him of your deeds within Skoironk.\n",
[11070]="70052E90\n1\tSet traps in the woods outside Hultvís (total: 12)\tTraps can be set outside Hultvís in Woodsedge. Wary of trusting any with his tale, Atta has asked you to set traps in the woods outside Hultvís.\n2\tTalk to Atta\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. You have set many traps in the woods outside Hultvís, and you should now return to Atta.\n",
[11071]="7005D3A6\n1\tDefeat and burn the remains of hill-wights at Skáilag\t\n2\tDefeat and burn the remains of hill-wights at Skáilag (total: 10)\tHill-wights can be found within Skáilag in Câr Bronach. Wrought long ago as a burial mound for the Hill-men of Rhudaur, servants of the Iron Crown have come to Skáilag to call forth the Dead that they might once more serve Angmar. You should defeat and burn the remains of hill-wights.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated and burned the remains of many hill-wights within Skáilag.\n",
[11072]="7005D3A5\n1\tCollect stolen Zhélruka trinkets from coffers at Skáilag\t\n2\tCollect stolen Zhélruka trinkets from coffers at Skáilag (total: 8)\tStolen Zhélruka trinkets might be found in coffers within Skáilag in Câr Bronach. Wrought long ago as a burial mound for the Hill-men of Rhudaur, servants of the Iron Crown have come to Skáilag to call forth the Dead that they might once more serve Angmar. You should search coffers in Skáilag for stolen Zhélruka trinkets.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have found several Zhélruka trinkets in the coffers of Skáilag.\n",
})
